# Git workflow (Stackward)

## Never push directly to `main`

All changes must go through a feature branch and pull request.

1. Create a descriptive branch from `main`, e.g. `cursor/phase-5-hardening` or `cursor/fix-ssh-retry`.
2. Commit on the feature branch.
3. Push the branch to `origin`.
4. Open a **draft PR** against `main`.
5. **Always request review from `alexseymer`** so the owner gets GitHub push notifications.

## Creating PRs

Prefer `gh pr create` with reviewer flag:

```bash
gh pr create \
  --base main \
  --head <branch> \
  --title "<title>" \
  --body "<body>" \
  --draft \
  --reviewer alexseymer
```

If using `ManagePullRequest` with `create_pr`, immediately assign the reviewer afterward:

```bash
gh pr edit <number> --add-reviewer alexseymer
```

## Do not

- `git push origin main` for feature work
- Merge PRs yourself unless the user explicitly asks
- Skip reviewer assignment — **always `alexseymer`**

## One-time: protect `main` on GitHub

The cloud agent cannot change branch protection (token lacks admin scope). A repo
admin must run this once after clone:

```bash
gh auth login   # as alexseymer
./scripts/protect-main-branch.sh
```

This enables PR + review + CI (`build`) requirements and blocks force-push/delete
on `main`. Alternative: add secret `GH_ADMIN_TOKEN` and run the
**Protect main branch** workflow from Actions.
